WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.755
You know that half second when you open

00:00:01.755 --> 00:00:03.420
your laptop to give Claude something,

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.238
and you hesitate and think,

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.360
where do I get started?

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.920
I'm Megan Choi, and I lead design for Claude Apps.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.924
Rolling out today, you don't have to

00:00:12.924 --> 00:00:14.660
pick between chat and co-work anymore.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.599
It's all one conversation,

00:00:16.599 --> 00:00:19.020
and Claude brings in whatever the task needs.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:21.953
Co-work is where we worked out how Claude

00:00:21.953 --> 00:00:24.020
should take on bigger, multi-step work.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:25.545
It got so good at deciding

00:00:25.545 --> 00:00:26.880
what a task actually needs,

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.317
keeping it in a separate place

00:00:28.317 --> 00:00:29.320
just stopped making sense.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.253
You no longer have to figure out where

00:00:31.253 --> 00:00:32.880
a task belongs before you start.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.221
And the capabilities of co-work are

00:00:35.221 --> 00:00:36.780
now more accessible everywhere.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.102
Your chats, tasks, skills,

00:00:39.102 --> 00:00:41.380
and memories are all still intact.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.780
Claude will meet you where the work is.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.180
Ask it a question or give it a bigger task.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.938
Or hand it last week's numbers and have

00:00:48.938 --> 00:00:50.820
it draft the deck or other visuals,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.560
and it'll build it all right there.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:54.600
It's all the same conversation now.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.220
The work comes back yours.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.282
You'll still be able to keep,

00:00:58.282 --> 00:01:00.700
edit, or steer any piece you want.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.220
This is the first step.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:03.912
As the models keep improving,

00:01:03.912 --> 00:01:05.780
we'll keep improving the experience as well.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:07.620
We'll bring you along as we go.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.000
Try it and let us know what you think.
